  "result": "I added `chunk<T>(items, size)` in `src/cli/chunk.ts` and committed it as \"Add a chunk helper that splits lists into fixed-size groups (t-6ja4q4u)\".\n\nIt splits a list into consecutive groups of `size`, and the last group can be shorter. It throws a `RangeError` for a size below 1. It also rejects non-integer and `NaN` sizes, which you didn't ask for, so a size like 1.5 can't slip through.\n\nThe new `test/cli/chunk.test.ts` has four tests, and all four pass when run on their own with `node --test`. They cover:\n- a normal split with a shorter last group\n- an empty list\n- a size larger than the list\n- invalid sizes\n\nI also added a weight of 0.1 for the new test file in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`, as the repo conventions require. I didn't run `npm run fast` or the full suite.",
